er  and at present tens of thousands of  homes are without power  yeah we've just been looking at some  images of that destruction ian  we mentioned that tornadoes are a rare  sight in these parts tell us more about  that  well they're extremely rare the tornado  we saw here yesterday in the czech  republic  was the kind of thing the kind of  twister people might more expect to see  somewhere like arizona in the united  states  but tornadoes of this kind aren't only  unusual  in this region in central europe they're  unusual in the whole of europe  apparently  in the last two decades they've only  been a couple of dozen  tornadoes of this force in europe and  the last  major tornado here in the czech republic  occurred in 2004  so a full 17 years ago  and ian just quickly are they gonna have  to appeal for for aid for this uh  cleanup operation  well the czech government is already  committing uh aid to help  the regions that are affected also there  has been aid from other countries these  slovaks and  uh austrians have sent  ambulances and rescue helicopters and  it's a really big operation  also what we've seen today is that there  have been several  uh public like charity collections to  help those who have been  impacted by this natural disaster  journalist ian willoughby speaking to us  uh thank you so much for that update
 

